Coupled Momentum-updated Memory Bank (CMMB)
In order to enrich the negative sample diversity and scale for both cellular and textual modalities, we follow [22, 50] to adopt the momentum update to build two coupled dynamic memory banks B c and B t , which are dedicated to preserving more cellular and textual features. The weights of these momentum encoders are adjusted dynamically based on their modality-specific encoders through momentum updates. For each latest training iteration, visual and textual instances are processed by the momentum encoders to generate corresponding embeddings, and these features are then stored in the coupled memory banks, which are implemented by utilizing the data structure of queue. The size of memory banks is represented by B .

